Dogfood Cloud v2 — the Slack-like Studio
========================================

#design #cloud #studio [[deploy-as-index-tree]]

The durable design record for the greenfield rewrite of the dogfood cloud
dashboard. Tracked as bd epic `wb-d8ac`. This file is the source of truth for
*why*; the bd issues are the source of truth for *what's left*.

design :studio_v2 do
  status "locked — 2026-06-25, grilled to shared understanding"
  epic   "wb-d8ac"
end


The diagnosis
-------------

The old dashboard (`app.js`, ~1,600 lines vanilla JS + 24 view modules, SSE,
per-view SWR) is slow in two specific ways, *not* a third:

- **B — inconsistent data load.** Every view hand-rolls its own fetch + SWR +
  invalidation. Lists/cards populate slowly and unevenly. This is the dominant
  complaint.
- **C — janky interactivity.** Imperative `innerHTML` churn; no reactive runtime
  keeping the DOM consistent as state changes.
- **NOT A — cold paint.** First paint is acceptable; a framework would not have
  been the fix on its own.

So the fix is a **reactivity model + a sync layer**, not merely a bundler.


The architecture
----------------

note :rendering do
  Client-driven rendering with a Solid-style **signals** runtime. The server
  never renders UI and never holds per-user UI state — cheapest, most
  horizontally-scalable posture. (Server-driven LiveView-style reactivity is a
  valid thing to build ON the platform, but wrong for THIS multi-tenant
  dashboard on cost grounds.)
end

note :sync do
  A generic **live-shapes** layer over WebSocket. Steals Electric SQL's *shape*
  abstraction — subscribe to a filtered row set, get a snapshot then a stream of
  deltas — but is built on `Nexus.Store` + the event bus + `Nexus.Live`, NOT on
  Electric itself (Electric is Postgres-coupled; our store is SQLite term-blobs,
  a hard mismatch). If `Nexus.Store` ever goes columnar/Postgres, real Electric
  becomes a drop-in — bridge intentionally not burned.

  - A subscription = `resource + workspace/channel equality filter`. Deliberately
    NOT arbitrary SQL, so fan-out stays cheap and access stays checkable.
  - `Nexus.Store.create/update` already emits `#event`; the WS layer broadcasts
    the delta to every client whose shape matches, after a server-side access
    check (workspace membership).
  - Presence / typing are ephemeral — a thin non-persisted side-channel, NOT
    resource-synced. Keeps the one heavy mechanism simple.
  - This single mechanism replaces all per-view SWR. Fixes B everywhere at once.
end

note :bundler do
  **Vite-in-washi** behind `work weave` for `client` islands. The client island
  stays plain JS that renders as-is in the browser — it is NOT compiled to wasm.
  The thing that runs in wasm is the bundler (the compiler), thesis-consistent.

  RISK / FIRST SPIKE (`wb-hyi8`): real Vite needs Node (Rollup/esbuild/fs/
  workers); the sandbox JS lane (quickjs-ng / go-yaegi) is insufficient. Likely
  start with **esbuild-wasm** as the "our-Vite" weave bundler — esbuild already
  ships a wasm build. Fallbacks: a Node-compat wasm runtime hosting real Vite,
  or host-native bundling as a transitional crutch. This is the single hardest
  technical piece and gates everything.
end

note :gleam do
  Set aside. Orthogonal language choice (Lustre client / server-side either way);
  revisit only after the shape above is shipping.
end


The product / information architecture
--------------------------------------

note :studio do
  Merge **apps + studio → one Studio**. A Slack-like explorer:
  - **Workspaces = the default grouping.** Sidebar groups everything by workspace.
  - **Rows, not cards.** Each row = icon/emoji + label. No avatar faces (for now).
    Compact, icon-and-color forward.
  - **Remove the agent splash.** Studio opens straight into team chat —
    modelled on Slack, not on an agent launcher.
end

note :unified_model do
  One **Surface / Channel** entity with a `kind` facet — `chat | agent | workflow
  | app`. A shared settings block (name, icon/emoji, purpose, workspace) is
  written ONCE and applies to every kind. Kind-specific data lives in a separate
  payload field (guards against a god-object). One row renderer, one settings
  panel, one access model, one sidebar grouping. DRY / least-code / componentize.
end

note :chat_center do
  **Hybrid, chat as centre of gravity.** Agents and workflows BOTH have a
  settings home (configure access/purpose/model) AND are summonable inside any
  chat — `@agent` to talk to one, `/workflow` to run one. The primary daily
  surface is team chat; the homes exist for configuration.
end

note :app_pages do
  The one kind with expandable children. An **app row expands to its pages**,
  sourced from the workbook's existing `app do section "…" do page "path/key"
  end end` block in its `index.work` (parsed by `Nexus.SSR.parse_app`). If no
  `app` block is declared, fall back to enumerating mounted surfaces / `route`
  registrations. Curated-by-author, free default. Pages inherit the app's
  workspace access.
end

note :access do
  **Access = workspace membership** for v1. A thing is usable by everyone in its
  workspace. Plus a single **private-to-me** flag for personal agent DMs (one
  human + agent). Per-channel custom member lists and full RBAC are deferred —
  designed so they slot in later without reworking the shape fan-out.
end

note :no_inbox do
  **There is no inbox.** Notifications/activity = messages an agent / system /
  workflow writes to a channel, riding the same live-shapes sync as human chat.
  - Events post to their **owning thing's channel** (a run posts to its workflow
    row's thread; an agent posts to the chat it ran in).
  - A per-workspace **`#system`** channel catches genuinely global events
    (deploys, billing, failures).
  - "Ping me" = **unread badge + @-mention**, computed client-side from synced
    messages. No server-side notification table.
  - Deletes the entire `/cloud/inbox` subsystem and the `hook :activity` →
    `resource :Event` path.
end


Strategy
--------

note :greenfield do
  **Greenfield**, not a strangler port. Justified BECAUSE this is a radical
  simplification (merge two views, unify four kinds into one, delete the inbox)
  rather than a 1:1 re-port — which removes greenfield's usual "reach parity"
  tail. The guard against that tail is a tight cutover scope (below).
end

note :v1_scope do
  v1 cutover = the minimum set that lets us turn the old dashboard off:
  - **Studio** (absorbs studio + apps): workspace-grouped rows, team chat,
    @-agents, /workflows, app rows → pages.
  - **Shared settings panel** for any row.
  - **Files** (port the workedit/CodeMirror island onto the new runtime).
  - **Data** (resource explorer — core).
  - **Minimal admin — NON-NEGOTIABLE:** secrets/env + team membership (the app
    is unoperable without them).
  Deferred / folded / dropped: runs (→ a thing's history, not a view), tasks/
  issues, toolkits, nexuses, inference, usage, storage, database.
end

flow :build_order do
  step :p0, run: "Phase 0 SPIKE (wb-hyi8): esbuild-wasm vs Vite weave bundler — one island bundled+hashed"
  step :p1, run: "Phase 1 (wb-q72x): signals runtime + weave wired into work dev (HMR), proven on one island"
  step :p2, run: "Phase 2 (wb-2sxb): live-shapes sync on Nexus.Store + WS, proven on resource :Message"
  step :p3, run: "Phase 3 (wb-wudl): greenfield Studio — Surface/kind model, rows, chat, @-agents, /workflows, app→pages, no-inbox"
  step :p4, run: "Phase 4 (wb-v4iw): port Files + Data + minimal admin (secrets/env + team)"
  step :p5, run: "Phase 5 (wb-56dx): cutover — retire app.js + 24 views, delete /cloud/inbox + hook:activity, verify green on wb-dogfood"
end
